<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64012" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λυγγούριον</span></b> , τό
		(derived by the ancients from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύγξ,
		οὖρον</span>, and supposed to be the coagulated urine of the lynx, <i><span class="en">
			Dsc.
			2.81
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Plu.
			2.962f
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			S.E.
			<u>P.</u>
			1.119
		</span></i>), a kind of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>amber</i>
			(glossed by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤλεκτρον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				4.6.2
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Lap.</u>
				28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				11(2).161
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				49
			</span></i> (Delos, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), al., <i><span class="en">
				22.1534.100
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				4.5.3
			</span></i> (pl.):—also written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λυγκούριον</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιγκούριον</span></b> , and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιγγούριον</span></b>  in codd.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λογγούριον</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				2.35
			</span></i>.</div>
